module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtStalkDual
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulQuotientStructureStalk

/-!
# The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient at a stalk, over the stalk of the quotient sheaf

Let `O♯` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a space, let `φ : (O♯)ʳ ⟶ O♯` generate a sheaf of
ideals, write `O_X` for the quotient of `O♯` by that sheaf of ideals, read as a sheaf of
commutative rings, and let `K` be a Koszul complex resolving `O_X`. At every point `x`,

`Ext^m_{O♯}(O_X, O_X)_x  ≅  ⋀ᵐ_{(O_X)_x}(Hom_{(O_X)_x}(((O_X)_x)ʳ, (O_X)_x))`,

the `m`-th exterior power, **over the stalk `(O_X)_x` of the quotient sheaf of rings**, of the dual
of a free module of rank `r`. In degree one this reads `Ext^1_x ≅ Hom_{(O_X)_x}(((O_X)_x)ʳ,
(O_X)_x)`, so the right-hand side above is the `m`-th exterior power of the degree-one answer,
which is the content of Stacks 0BQY at a stalk.

The three identifications composed are the stalk identification of the Ext sheaf as the
`O_x`-linear maps out of the stalk of an exterior power; the identification of the stalk of the
cokernel of `φ` with `(O_X)_x`, linearly over `O_x`; and the base-change identification of
`O_x`-linear maps into an `O_x`-algebra with linear functionals on the exterior power formed over
that algebra, the algebra being `(O_X)_x` along the stalk of the quotient map.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extStructureStalkDualEquiv`: the identification
  displayed above.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.ext1StructureStalkDualEquiv`: its degree-one case.

## Implementation notes

**This supersedes the `O_x ⧸ J_x` form for downstream use.**
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extStalkDualEquiv` states the same identification with the
exterior power formed over the quotient `O_x ⧸ J_x` of the stalk of `O♯` by the ideal generated by
the germs of the generators. That ring is identified with `(O_X)_x` only as an `O_x`-module, by
`Stacks.RegularSequence.quotientStalkEquiv`; the ring-level identification, which is what an
exterior power formed over it would need, is a separate matter. The source side of the comparison
of Stacks 0BQY — the stalk of `⋀ᵐ_{O_X}(Ext^1)`, formed over `O_X` — is natively an exterior power
over `(O_X)_x`, so it is the form given here that meets it, and no ring-level comparison of two
presentations of the quotient is required anywhere.

What makes the restatement possible with no new mathematical input is that
`exteriorPower.exteriorDualFreeBaseChangeEquiv` takes an **arbitrary** `R`-algebra `S`, not a
quotient of `R`; `Stacks.RegularSequence.quotientStalkAlgebra` supplies the algebra structure on
`(O_X)_x` over `O_x`, and `Stacks.RegularSequence.cokernelStalkLinearEquivStructureStalk` is the
`O_x`-linear identification of the coefficient module.

**The composite is an equivalence of types, not a linear equivalence**, for the reason recorded in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtStalkDual`: the three factors are linear
over different rings, the first two over `O_x` and the third over `(O_X)_x`, and a module over
`(O_X)_x` is not thereby a module over `O_x`. Each factor retains its own linearity and can be
used separately where that is wanted; what consumes the composite is a bijectivity statement.

**The algebra structure is introduced with `letI` and the target type is ascribed inside it.**
`Stacks.RegularSequence.quotientStalkAlgebra` is a definition rather than an instance, so a
binder type mentioning an exterior power over `(O_X)_x` written before it is in scope fails
instance search for `Module ↑(ringStalk Rc x) ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)`. Ascribing the
type inside the `letI` is the idiom of
`Stacks.RegularSequence.unitStalkBaseLinearEquiv` and is what makes these elaborate.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex Stacks.ChainComplex

universe u

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

open Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.SheafOfModules.SheafHomStalk Stacks.RegularSequence

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) CommRingCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ}
  {A : SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)}
  {φ : koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)}

/-- **The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient at a stalk are exterior powers over the stalk
of the quotient sheaf of rings.** At a point `x`, the stalk of `Ext^m_{O♯}(O_X, O_X)` is the `m`-th
exterior power over `(O_X)_x` of the dual of the free `(O_X)_x`-module of rank `r`.

The composite is of the stalk identification of the Ext sheaf, the `O_x`-linear identification of
the stalk of the cokernel of `φ` with `(O_X)_x`, and the base-change identification of
`O_x`-linear maps into the `O_x`-algebra `(O_X)_x` with `(O_X)_x`-linear functionals on the
exterior power formed over `(O_X)_x`.

This supersedes `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extStalkDualEquiv`, which states the
same identification over the quotient `O_x ⧸ J_x` of the stalk of `O♯`, for every downstream use:
the source of the comparison of Stacks 0BQY is an exterior power over `O_X`, whose stalk is
natively an exterior power over `(O_X)_x`. -/
def extStructureStalkDualEquiv (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) [QuasiIso K.augmentation]
    (m : ℕ) (x : X) :=
  letI := quotientStalkAlgebra Rc φ x
  (((extStalkEquiv Rc K m x).toEquiv.trans
      (LinearEquiv.arrowCongr (LinearEquiv.refl (ringStalk Rc x) _)
        (cokernelStalkLinearEquivStructureStalk Rc φ x)).toEquiv).trans
    (exteriorPower.exteriorDualFreeBaseChangeEquiv ↑(ringStalk Rc x)
      ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x) (Fin r) m).toEquiv.symm :
    modStalk
        (derivedSheafExt Rc
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))) ((m : ℕ) : ℤ)) x ≃
      ⋀[↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)]^m
        (Module.Dual ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)
          (Fin r → ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x))))

/-- **The first Ext sheaf at a stalk is the dual of a free module of rank `r` over the stalk of
the quotient sheaf of rings.** This is `extStructureStalkDualEquiv` in degree one, with the first
exterior power of a module identified with the module itself. So the stalk of `Ext^1` is free of
rank `r` over `(O_X)_x`, and the target of `extStructureStalkDualEquiv` is the `m`-th exterior
power of it. -/
def ext1StructureStalkDualEquiv (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) [QuasiIso K.augmentation]
    (x : X) :=
  letI := quotientStalkAlgebra Rc φ x
  ((extStructureStalkDualEquiv Rc K 1 x).trans
    (exteriorPower.oneEquiv ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)
      (Module.Dual ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)
        (Fin r → ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)))).toEquiv :
    modStalk
        (derivedSheafExt Rc
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))) ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) x ≃
      Module.Dual ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)
        (Fin r → ↑(quotientStructureStalk Rc φ x)))

end Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

end
